{
  "header": [
    "CONTROL-SET — the peers whose behaviour on a requirement has been OBSERVED, so that a new suite's",
    "first run can be checked against a declared expectation instead of against somebody's memory.",
    "",
    "⛔⛔ THIS FILE IS NOT READABLE BY A SUITE AUTHOR. It contains the answers. An author who reads it",
    "builds a suite that agrees with this one for reasons that have nothing to do with the protocol,",
    "which is the exact failure this repo exists to prevent. It is the VALIDATOR's artifact, consumed",
    "AFTER a new suite has run, never before. docs/BRIEF-SUITE-2.md lists it as forbidden.",
    "",
    "⛔ AND IT IS A COMPARISON SET, NEVER AN ANSWER KEY. A new suite disagreeing with a row here is",
    "exactly one of three things — the specification was ambiguous, the peer is wrong, or ONE OF THE",
    "TWO SUITES IS WRONG — and finding out which is the entire job. The moment a row here is treated as",
    "the correct answer, suite 1 has become the oracle and the second suite is a slow copy of it.",
    "",
    "WHY IT EXISTS. Operator direction, 2026-09-16: a bring-up chunk must not be built against",
    "requirements whose answers we do not already know, because a suite reporting FAIL everywhere and a",
    "suite that is simply broken produce IDENTICAL OUTPUT. A requirement is fit for bring-up only when",
    "BOTH of its outcome classes have been observed on real peers.",
    "",
    "⚠ THE INDEPENDENCE OF THIS DATA IS BOUNDED AND THE BOUND IS STATED PER ROW. These are one",
    "instrument's readings of a peer's wire behaviour. The OBSERVATION (what bytes came back) is strong;",
    "the VERDICT (whether that satisfies the obligation) carries this seat's judgement and is exactly",
    "what a second suite exists to challenge."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "taken": "2026-09-16",
  "instrument": {
    "suite": "py-prototype",
    "version": "0b82019",
    "source_digest": "d594454c3f0c54795b7bd97b",
    "note": [
      "⭐ FIXED DURING THE REVIEW PASS THAT PRODUCED THIS FILE. The rows were first recorded under",
      "`844a454-dirty`, and that string is NOT AN IDENTITY: it names a commit that does not contain the",
      "checks that ran — the bundle was built from a dirty tree later committed as `135bed9`, so a reader",
      "resolving it gets the PREVIOUS ECP-R3 check, the one that passed the defect. Worse, `git describe`",
      "is a dependency of no file, so `make build` on a CLEAN tree was a no-op while BUILD.json kept the",
      "stale dirty string — the identity could not be corrected by rebuilding.",
      "",
      "⇒ `source_digest` is sha256 over the 12 bundled suite source files. It cannot go stale and cannot",
      "be bumped without the code moving. Every row below was re-measured under it.",
      "",
      "⚠ Note the shape: this is the THIRD instance in one day of a NAME standing in for CONTENT —",
      "a spec version header that did not move, a per-peer version pin that went stale, and an instrument",
      "id that named the wrong commit. Two were routed to other seats; this one was ours."
    ]
  },
  "staleness": [
    "⛔ EVERY ROW CARRIES THE sha256 OF THE REQUIREMENT FILE IT WAS MEASURED AGAINST, AND THAT IS THE",
    "WHOLE POINT OF THE FILE. `tools/control-set-gate.py` recomputes each digest from `requirements/`",
    "every run and FAILS when a row's obligation has moved underneath it.",
    "",
    "⭐ THIS RULE WAS EARNED THE SAME HOUR THE FILE WAS WRITTEN. The first draft of this control set was",
    "built from the 06:42 run and recorded `ECP-R3: 3 PASS on the generator peers`. Those verdicts were",
    "scored against requirement text that no longer exists — measured, not suspected: ECP-R3 was",
    "`9714ce72…` in that run and is `08155caf…` at HEAD, and ECP-R7 and ECP-R57 had BOTH moved too.",
    "The re-authoring of ECP-R3 landed between the two runs. ⇒ A control set that records a verdict",
    "without the obligation's digest is AP-18 with the blast radius pointed at the validator: it would",
    "have told a new suite that three peers pass a rule none of them had been measured against.",
    "",
    "⇒ EVERY PEER BELOW WAS RE-RUN AFTER THAT POINT, SO EVERY ROW SHARES ONE OBLIGATION TEXT WITH HEAD."
  ],
