  "peer_drift": [
    "⛔⭐ THE COHORT MOVED UNDER US INSIDE ONE WORKING DAY, AND THE PIN IS WHAT MADE IT VISIBLE RATHER",
    "THAN CONFUSING. RESOLVED AND RE-PINNED — the history is kept because it is the evidence.",
    "",
    "Four runs. Same obligations after 11:18; the instrument's identity was corrected at 13:29:",
    "",
    "  06:42  generator @ 38f961b3 dirty   ECP-R57  4 of 4 FAIL   ⚠ scored against OLD requirement text",
    "  13:03  generator @ 38f961b3 dirty   ECP-R57  2 PASS/2 FAIL",
    "  13:24  generator @ ac93a1cd CLEAN   ECP-R57  2 PASS/2 FAIL",
    "  13:29  generator @ ac93a1cd dirty   ECP-R57  2 PASS/2 FAIL   ← the rows below, under the",
    "                                                                 REBUILT instrument 0b82019",
    "",
    "The three generator peers sat on ONE git head (`38f961b3`) across the first two runs, so a reader",
    "tracking the cohort by commit would have seen nothing move and would have been wrong. What",
    "separated them was the uncommitted-diff digest:",
    "",
    "  python-content      dirty c7a2a0cf…   FAIL(silent_drop) → PASS(400 invalid_request)",
    "  typescript-content  dirty 98a08a92…   FAIL(bare_close)  → PASS(400 invalid_request)",
    "  rust-content        CLEAN             FAIL(silent_drop) → unchanged",
    "",
    "⇒ THE TWO PEERS WITH UNCOMMITTED EDITS IMPROVED AND THE CLEAN ONE DID NOT. That is the F50 hazard",
    "measured instead of feared, and the same shape as the version-header finding routed to arch today:",
    "A COMMIT IS NOT A CONTENT DIGEST.",
    "",
    "⛔ AND 'DURABLE' WAS THE WRONG WORD FOR ABOUT TWENTY MINUTES — CORRECTED HERE RATHER THAN QUIETLY.",
    "At 13:24 the generator committed those edits as `ac93a1c` (their W-18), the tree was CLEAN, and",
    "this file said every peer was now pinned to a committed artifact. By 13:29 the tree was dirty",
    "again — nine `SYSTEM.toml` files and `tools/check-expectation.py`, which is THEM implementing the",
    "requirement-keyed gate baselines this seat asked them for. **A counterpart's tree is not a thing",
    "that becomes clean and stays clean**, and a control set that waits for one will never be written.",
    "",
    "⭐⭐ SO THE DURABILITY ARGUMENT IS REPETITION, NOT CLEANLINESS, AND IT IS THE STRONGER ONE ANYWAY.",
    "These verdicts have now been produced FOUR TIMES across THREE DIFFERENT PEER-TREE STATES —",
    "dirty `c7a2a0cf…`, clean `ac93a1c`, dirty `165481eb…` — and they did not move. A single clean pin",
    "is one observation; the same answer across changing peer bytes is evidence the answer is about the",
    "PEER and not about the moment. The pins below are recorded exactly as measured, point-in-time,",
    "and the run that produced each one is named.",
    "",
    "⭐⭐ AND THE FINDING THAT CAME OUT OF IT IS ROUTABLE AND IS NOT A COMPLAINT — see `w18_blind_spot`.",
    "",
    "⛔ THE PRIOR MEASUREMENTS ARE GONE FROM `output/`. Each run overwrites the provenance in place, so",
    "the 06:42 and 13:03 peer pins cannot be recovered from the tree. The before-values above survive",
    "ONLY because this file copied them by hand. Run artifacts are not retained — filed as a gap, not",
    "fixed, and it is a real one for a seat whose product is comparability."
  ],
  "w18_blind_spot": [
    "⭐⭐ A BEHAVIOUR CHANGE LANDED ON A RULE THE CHANGE'S OWN CONTROL COULD NOT SEE. Routable to",
    "`entity-system-generator`, and it is generous rather than accusatory: THEY NAMED THIS CLASS",
    "THEMSELVES IN THE SAME COMMIT.",
    "",
    "Their `ac93a1c` (W-18) replaced nine hand-copied peer hosts with keystone's `run_host`. Their",
    "control, quoted from the commit: *\"Pre-port reports were snapshotted before the first rebuild, then",
    "compared per (file, category, name) across six compositions, both arms, two rounds: 0 SEVERITIES",
    "MOVED OF 20,280 OBSERVATIONS, with identical check sets — nothing appeared and nothing vanished.\"*",
    "",
    "⛔ BUT ECP-R57 AND ECP-R3 ARE **ORACLE BLIND** — verified in `output/DIFFERENTIAL.md` on all four",
    "peers, regenerated 2026-09-16 13:30: `validate-peer` executes NO check that joins either",
    "requirement, so a 20,280-observation severity diff over its reports CANNOT CONTAIN A ROW FOR",
    "EITHER. Their control is correct within its instrument and its instrument is blind here.",
    "",
    "⚠ WHAT WE CAN AND CANNOT ATTRIBUTE, STATED PRECISELY BECAUSE THE TEMPTATION IS TO OVERCLAIM:",
    "",
    "  ESTABLISHED  two generator peers changed ECP-R57 behaviour inside the window of their change,",
    "               measured both before and after, and the only edit in that window was W-18's.",
    "  ESTABLISHED  a severity diff over validate-peer reports could not have seen it either way.",
    "  NOT ESTABLISHED  that W-18 CAUSED it. Their own message says `rust` was ported to `run_host` on",
    "               2026-09-13 — three days before — AND RUST DID NOT MOVE. If the port were sufficient,",
    "               rust should also have moved. Their message names a per-substrate difference in",
    "               rust's integration, which is consistent with this and does not prove it. THE BISECT",
    "               IS THEIRS; we can say when it moved, not why.",
    "",
    "⭐ THE REASON TO SEND IT: their own commit already says *\"the severity diff is structurally blind to",
    "what nearly broke … a silent loss would have moved no severity and failed no gate\"* — they found",
    "one instance of that class themselves and re-hooked it. THIS IS A SECOND INSTANCE OF THE SAME",
    "CLASS, found from outside, on the conformance surface itself. A change that improves a peer is the",
    "friendly version of the finding; the same blind spot passes a regression."
  ],
  "durable_means": [
    "⭐ `durable: true` ON AN EXPECTATION MEANS THE VERDICT HAS BEEN REPRODUCED ACROSS DIFFERENT PEER",
    "BYTES — not that the peer is pinned to a commit. The generator's tree is under active development",
    "and will be dirty most times you look at it; waiting for a clean pin is waiting forever. Every",
    "expectation below was produced FOUR TIMES across THREE peer-tree states and did not move.",
    "",
    "⛔ WHAT IT DOES NOT MEAN: that the verdict will hold tomorrow. Two of these peers changed behaviour",
    "on ECP-R57 THIS MORNING. Re-run before trusting a row that matters, and if a row moves, that is",
    "data about the peer — not a reason to edit this file quietly."
  ],
