      "why_unfit": "⛔ WITHDRAWN 2026-09-16 (c), and NOT because a peer moved. The obligation this row scores against was falsified by ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL 0.8.2.28, which added to §4.11's cause table the exact row ECP-R3's reading argues does not exist: `root entity self-consistency -> 400 hash_mismatch`, and split arm (4) into (4a) resolution integrity and (4b) root self-consistency so a check can drive each alone. The OBSERVATIONS below stand — they are what came back on the wire. The EXPECTATIONS do not: `rust-content` answered `non_canonical_ecf` and is recorded PASS here on the argument that no code is pinned. Under .28 a code is pinned and that peer is answering the wrong one. ⇒ 1 of 4 expectations inverts, and it is not safe to hand a new suite a comparison set we know is wrong for a quarter of its rows. Re-measure against a re-authored ECP-R3, then restore.",
